{"type":"excalidraw","version":2,"source":"https://app.excalidraw.com","metadata":{"id":"9iXTH36cGDi","workspace":"4c8x9O2Yp2e","name":"Untitled scene","created":"2026-06-23T20:50:29.329Z","updated":"2026-06-23T20:54:12.718Z","collection":null,"creator":"2ElKsXERQIc","updater":"2ElKsXERQIc","isPrivate":true,"pinned":false},"elements":[{"id":"gut2A2iy-RbiafIDq1D97","type":"rectangle","x":506.92578125,"y":177.87109375,"width":414.42578125000006,"height":154.30859375,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"index":"a0","roundness":{"type":3},"seed":1046559167,"version":76,"versionNonce":1516492159,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[{"type":"text","id":"iDDYqm5Uh6BtuX_436ybI"}],"updated":1782247839632,"link":null,"locked":false},{"id":"iDDYqm5Uh6BtuX_436ybI","type":"text","x":621.2987518310547,"y":217.525390625,"width":185.67984008789062,"height":75,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"index":"a1","roundness":null,"seed":1081847825,"version":59,"versionNonce":924711057,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":null,"updated":1782247849408,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"product_commission\n- effective_from \n- effective _to ","fontSize":20,"fontFamily":6,"textAlign":"center","verticalAlign":"middle","containerId":"gut2A2iy-RbiafIDq1D97","originalText":"product_commission\n- effective_from \n- effective _to ","autoResize":true,"lineHeight":1.25},{"id":"h1YsQ-IcfrxqZ7l5gdw7C","type":"text","x":692.3653493027914,"y":433.5,"width":1312.21484375,"height":1225,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"index":"a2","roundness":null,"seed":896051217,"version":5,"versionNonce":1006732959,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":null,"updated":1782248042963,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"const FALLBACK_RATE = 10;\n\n  type RateVersion = { effectiveFrom: string; commissionRate: string | null };\n\n  // Latest version (by effectiveFrom) that matches `match` and is in effect by `eventDate`.\n  // null if the latest match is a tombstone, or nothing matches → caller falls through.\n  function latestRate<T extends RateVersion>(\n    versions: T[],\n    match: (v: T) => boolean,\n      if (!match(v)) continue;\n      if (v.effectiveFrom <= eventDate && (!best || v.effectiveFrom > best.effectiveFrom)) best = v;\n    }\n    return best && best.commissionRate !== null ? Number(best.commissionRate) : null;\n  }\n\n  function effectiveRate(f: Fact, pc: PcVersion[], bc: BcVersion[]): number {\n    const d = f.eventDate;\n    return (\n      (f.creatorAccountId !== null\n        ? latestRate(pc, (v) => v.retailerProductId === f.retailerProductId && v.creatorAccountId === f.creatorAccountId, d)\n        : null) ??                                                                              // creator override\n    return (\n      creatorRate ??                                                              // 1. creator override\n      asOfRate(pcByKey.get(`${f.retailerProductId}:null`) ?? [], f.eventDate) ??  // 2. product default\n      asOfRate(bcByAccount.get(f.brandAccountId) ?? [], f.eventDate) ??           // 3. brand default\n      FALLBACK_RATE                                                               // 4. 10%\n    );\n  }\n\n  Worked trace showing the nulls in action\n\n  Loaded data for product 10 / account 7 (ATTRIBUTION):\n  pc = [\n    { retailerProductId:10, creatorAccountId:null, commissionRate:\"15.00\", effectiveFrom:\"2026-01-01\" },\n    { retailerProductId:10, creatorAccountId:null, commissionRate:null,    effectiveFrom:\"2026-05-01\" }, // product default CLEARED\n    { retailerProductId:10, creatorAccountId:99,   commissionRate:\"20.00\", effectiveFrom:\"2026-03-01\" },\n  ]\n  bc = [ { accountId:7, commissionRate:\"12.00\", effectiveFrom:\"2026-01-01\" } ]\n\n  - Fact A — product 10, creator 99, eventDate \"2026-06-01\":\n  asOfRate(creator 99) → latest ≤ Jun 1 is the 20.00 (Mar 1) → 20%. Done. (commission = sales × 0.20)\n  - Fact B — product 10, creator null, eventDate \"2026-06-01\":\n  creator step skipped → asOfRate(product default) → latest ≤ Jun 1 is the tombstone (May 1, null) → null → fall through → asOfRate(brand 7) →\n  12.00 → 12%. (the cleared product default correctly hands off to the brand default)\n  - Fact C — product 10, creator null, eventDate \"2026-04-15\" (before the clear):\n  asOfRate(product default) → latest ≤ Apr 15 is 15.00 (Jan 1) → 15%. (the old product rate still prices pre-clear sales — reproducibility)\n\n  So ?? walks creator → product → brand → 10%, and at each level a null (tombstone or absent) is what advances to the next — which is exactly\n  why the load must keep the tombstone rows in pc/bc.","fontSize":20,"fontFamily":6,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"originalText":"const FALLBACK_RATE = 10;\n\n  type RateVersion = { effectiveFrom: string; commissionRate: string | null };\n\n  // Latest version (by effectiveFrom) that matches `match` and is in effect by `eventDate`.\n  // null if the latest match is a tombstone, or nothing matches → caller falls through.\n  function latestRate<T extends RateVersion>(\n    versions: T[],\n    match: (v: T) => boolean,\n      if (!match(v)) continue;\n      if (v.effectiveFrom <= eventDate && (!best || v.effectiveFrom > best.effectiveFrom)) best = v;\n    }\n    return best && best.commissionRate !== null ? Number(best.commissionRate) : null;\n  }\n\n  function effectiveRate(f: Fact, pc: PcVersion[], bc: BcVersion[]): number {\n    const d = f.eventDate;\n    return (\n      (f.creatorAccountId !== null\n        ? latestRate(pc, (v) => v.retailerProductId === f.retailerProductId && v.creatorAccountId === f.creatorAccountId, d)\n        : null) ??                                                                              // creator override\n    return (\n      creatorRate ??                                                              // 1. creator override\n      asOfRate(pcByKey.get(`${f.retailerProductId}:null`) ?? [], f.eventDate) ??  // 2. product default\n      asOfRate(bcByAccount.get(f.brandAccountId) ?? [], f.eventDate) ??           // 3. brand default\n      FALLBACK_RATE                                                               // 4. 10%\n    );\n  }\n\n  Worked trace showing the nulls in action\n\n  Loaded data for product 10 / account 7 (ATTRIBUTION):\n  pc = [\n    { retailerProductId:10, creatorAccountId:null, commissionRate:\"15.00\", effectiveFrom:\"2026-01-01\" },\n    { retailerProductId:10, creatorAccountId:null, commissionRate:null,    effectiveFrom:\"2026-05-01\" }, // product default CLEARED\n    { retailerProductId:10, creatorAccountId:99,   commissionRate:\"20.00\", effectiveFrom:\"2026-03-01\" },\n  ]\n  bc = [ { accountId:7, commissionRate:\"12.00\", effectiveFrom:\"2026-01-01\" } ]\n\n  - Fact A — product 10, creator 99, eventDate \"2026-06-01\":\n  asOfRate(creator 99) → latest ≤ Jun 1 is the 20.00 (Mar 1) → 20%. Done. (commission = sales × 0.20)\n  - Fact B — product 10, creator null, eventDate \"2026-06-01\":\n  creator step skipped → asOfRate(product default) → latest ≤ Jun 1 is the tombstone (May 1, null) → null → fall through → asOfRate(brand 7) →\n  12.00 → 12%. (the cleared product default correctly hands off to the brand default)\n  - Fact C — product 10, creator null, eventDate \"2026-04-15\" (before the clear):\n  asOfRate(product default) → latest ≤ Apr 15 is 15.00 (Jan 1) → 15%. (the old product rate still prices pre-clear sales — reproducibility)\n\n  So ?? walks creator → product → brand → 10%, and at each level a null (tombstone or absent) is what advances to the next — which is exactly\n  why the load must keep the tombstone rows in pc/bc.","autoResize":true,"lineHeight":1.25}],"appState":{"viewBackgroundColor":"#ffffff","lockedMultiSelections":{}},"files":{}}